_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 13
---
order: 13
---
short_label: XIII.13
---
red_highlight: yes
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: To construct a pyramid, to comprehend it in a given sphere; and to prove that the square on the diameter of the sphere is one and a half times the square on the side of the pyramid.
----
proof:

Set out the diameter {AB} of the given sphere, cut it at the point {C} so that {AC} is double {CB}, describe the semicircle {ADB|semiT} on {AB}, draw {CD} from the point {C} at right angles to {AB}, and join {DA}. [!just VI.9; I.11]

Set out the circle {EFG|EFGc} with radius equal to {DC}, inscribe the equilateral triangle {EFG} in the circle {EFG|EFGc}, take the center {H} of the circle, and join {EH}, {HF}, and {HG}. [!just I.1; IV.2]

Set {HK} up from the point {H} at right angles to the plane of the circle {EFG|EFGc}, cut off {HK} equal to the straight line {AC} from {HK}, and join {KE}, {KF}, and {KG}. [!just XI.12; I.3]

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="440" height="280" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="XIII.13 diagram" src="propXIII13.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // The walk builds the tetrahedron in the order the proof does: the
    // semicircle on AB with C, D, then the circle EFG on radius DC with its
    // inscribed triangle, HK up from the plane and the joins to K; then HL
    // produced, the semicircle on KL through E, carried round to sweep out
    // the sphere through F and G.
    //
    // Joyce's figure draws the triangle EFG and the joins KE, KF, KG only as
    // edges of the polyhedron EFGK, and HK, HL only as the one line KL, so
    // EFG (faceless outline), KE, KF, KG, HK and HL are solid slide twins,
    // hidden at rest (initiallyHidden); EFGK joins the walk once the pyramid
    // is constructed and KL once HL is produced. A polyhedron and a sphere draw no highlight,
    // so pEFGK is a faceless octagon wireframe walking the six edges and sphT
    // a faceless circle on the sphere's outline. The circle EFG carries the
    // default opaque face, so the walk draws EFGc, a solid faceless twin
    // hidden at rest, and keeps EFGcirc out of the slide sets; semiT is a
    // faceless twin of the filled semicircle ADB (#140). A sector
    // draws only in the screen plane, so the semicircle on KL is lit as the
    // great circle it lies on, in the plane through E (KELc), and through F
    // and G once it is carried round (KFLc, KGLc).
    // Everything else added is transparent.
    //
    // Draggables (checked against the bundle): A, B (lineSliders, givens),
    // M (free; the sphere's centre), K (sphereSlider), E (circleSlider).
    // M, K and E arrive mid-walk and are deferred. C, D, H, L, F, G are
    // derived and listed per slide.
    var GIVEN = ["A","B","AB"];
    var CUT   = GIVEN.concat(["C","AC","CB"]);
    var SEMI  = CUT.concat(["semi","semiT"]);
    var PERP  = SEMI.concat(["D","CD","angACD"]);
    var JDA   = PERP.concat(["AD"]);
    var CIRC  = JDA.concat(["EFGc"]);
    var TRI   = CIRC.concat(["E","F","G","EFG","EF","FG","GE"]);
    var CEN   = TRI.concat(["H","HE","HF","HG"]);
    var UP    = CEN.concat(["K","HK"]);
    var JK    = UP.concat(["KE","KF","KG"]);
    var RT    = JK.concat(["angKHE","angKHF","angKHG"]);
    var FOUR  = RT.concat(["KEF","KFG","KEG","pEFGK"]);
    var PYR   = FOUR.concat(["EFGK"]);
    // The sphere half: the markers at H other than KHE have done their work.
    var BASE  = JK.concat(["angKHE","KEF","KFG","KEG","pEFGK","EFGK"]);
    var PROD  = BASE.concat(["L","HL"]);
    var DIAM  = PROD.concat(["KL"]);
    var RT2   = DIAM.concat(["angEHL"]);
    var ARC   = RT2.concat(["KELc"]);
    var SPH   = ARC.concat(["M","Msphere","sphT"]);
    var ROUND = SPH.concat(["KFLc","KGLc","FL","LG","angKFL","angKGL"]);
    var FIN   = SPH;
    var REST  = ["A","B","AB","semi","semiT","C","D","CD","AD","M","Msphere","sphT",
                 "K","L","H","KL","EFGcirc","EFGc","E","F","G","EFGK","pEFGK",
                 "HE","HF","HG","EF"];
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "XIII.13",
        elements: [
            "A0;point;free;40,-1000;0;0",
            "A3;point;free;40,1000;0;0",
            "A;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,0,40",
            "B;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,0,250",
            "AB;line;connect;A,B",
            "ABmid;point;midpoint;A,B;0;0",
            "ABcirc;circle;radius;ABmid,B;0;0;0;0",
            "semi;sector;sector;ABmid,B,A;0;0;black;random",
