            { text: "also equals each of the straight lines {KE}, {KF}, and {KG}.",
              visible: RT,
              highlighted: ["EF","FG","GE","KE","KF","KG"] },
            { text: "Therefore the four triangles {EFG}, {KEF}, {KFG}, and {KEG} are equilateral.",
              visible: FOUR,
              highlighted: ["EFG","KEF","KFG","KEG"] },
            { text: "Therefore a pyramid has been constructed out of four equilateral triangles,",
              visible: PYR,
              highlighted: ["pEFGK"] },
            { text: "the triangle {EFG} being its base and the point {K} its vertex.",
              visible: PYR,
              highlighted: ["EFG","K"] },
            { text: "It is next required to comprehend it in the given sphere",
              visible: BASE,
              highlighted: ["pEFGK","AB"] },
            { text: "and to prove that the square on the diameter of the sphere",
              visible: BASE,
              highlighted: ["AB"] },
            { text: "is one and a half times the square on the side of the pyramid.",
              visible: BASE,
              highlighted: ["AB","EF"] },
            { text: "Produce the straight line {HL} in a straight line with {KH}, and make {HL} equal to {CB}.",
              visible: PROD,
              highlighted: ["HL","HK","CB"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "HL", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeExtend },
                  { elem: "L", name: geomlib.A.Point.appear } ] },
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.3" }] },
            { text: "Now, since {AC} is to {CD} as {CD} is to {CB},",
              visible: DIAM,
              highlighted: ["AC","CD","CB"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "VI.8.Cor" }] },
            { text: "while {AC} equals {KH}, {CD} equals {HE}, and {CB} equals {HL},",
              visible: DIAM,
              highlighted: ["AC","HK","CD","HE","CB","HL"] },
            { text: "therefore {KH} is to {HE} as {EH} is to {HL}.",
              visible: DIAM,
              highlighted: ["HK","HE","HL"] },
            { text: "Therefore the rectangle {KH} by {HL} equals the square on {EH}.",
              visible: DIAM,
              highlighted: ["HK","HL","HE"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "VI.17" }] },
            { text: "And each of the angles {KHE}, {EHL} is right,",
              visible: RT2,
              highlighted: ["angKHE","angEHL"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "angEHL", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] } },
            { text: "therefore the semicircle described on {KL} passes through {E} also.",
              visible: ARC,
              highlighted: ["KELc","KL","E"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "VI.8" }, { ref: "III.31" }] },
            { text: "If then, {KL} remaining fixed, the semicircle is carried round",
              visible: ARC,
              highlighted: ["KL","KELc"] },
            { text: "and restored to the same position from which it began to be moved,",
              visible: SPH,
              highlighted: ["sphT"] },
            { text: "then it also passes through the points {F} and {G},",
              visible: SPH,
              highlighted: ["F","G","KFLc","KGLc"] },
            { text: "since, if {FL} and {LG} are joined, then the angles at {F} and {G} similarly become right angles,",
              visible: ROUND,
              highlighted: ["FL","LG","angKFL","angKGL"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "angKFL", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angKGL", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] } },
            { text: "and the pyramid is comprehended in the given sphere.",
              visible: FIN,
              highlighted: ["pEFGK","sphT"] },
            { text: "For {KL}, the diameter of the sphere, equals the diameter {AB} of the given sphere,",
              visible: FIN,
              highlighted: ["KL","AB"] },
            { text: "since {KH} was made equal to {AC}, and {HL} to {CB}.",
              visible: FIN,
              highlighted: ["HK","AC","HL","CB"] },
            { text: "I say next that the square on the diameter of the sphere",
              visible: FIN,
              highlighted: ["KL"] },
            { text: "is one and a half times the square on the side of the pyramid.",
              visible: FIN,
              highlighted: ["KL","EF"] },
            { text: "Since {AC} is double {CB}, therefore {AB} is triple {BC},",
              visible: FIN,
              highlighted: ["AC","CB","AB"] },
            { text: "and, in conversion, {BA} is one and a half times {AC}.",
              visible: FIN,
              highlighted: ["AB","AC"] },
            { text: "But {BA} is to {AC} as the square on {BA} is to the square on {AD}.",
              visible: FIN,
              highlighted: ["AB","AC","AD"] },
            { text: "Therefore the square on {BA} is also one and a half times the square on {AD}.",
              visible: FIN,
              highlighted: ["AB","AD"] },
            { text: "And {BA} is the diameter of the given sphere, and {AD} equals the side of the pyramid.",
              visible: FIN,
              highlighted: ["AB","AD","EF"] },
            { text: "Therefore the square on the diameter of the sphere",
              visible: FIN,
              highlighted: ["KL","AB"] },
            { text: "is one and a half times the square on the side of the pyramid.",
              visible: FIN,
              highlighted: ["KL","EF","AD"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "Q.E.F." }] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            if (ref === "XIII.13") return "#prop";
